# Chimera — environment configuration template.
#
# STATUS: Chimera currently reads NO environment variables.
#
# Nothing in `chimera/`, `tests/`, or `demo_app/` calls `os.environ` or
# `os.getenv`, and there is no dotenv loader. All policy, paths, and
# timeouts are constants in code (see `chimera/agent.py` DEFAULT_POLICY
# and `chimera/safety.py` RetryPolicy).
#
# This file therefore declares no settings. It exists so the
# configuration surface is explicit and reviewable rather than implicit
# (SRS NFR-025, and the repository layout in SRS §16).
#
# To add a variable:
#   1. Declare it below with a placeholder value — never a real credential.
#   2. Read it as `os.environ.get(NAME, DEFAULT)` with a documented
#      default, so the project still runs with no `.env` file present.
#   3. Document it in `docs/user_guide.md` §14.
#   4. Commit the variable's NAME here; never commit its value.
#
# Model-provider API keys are deliberately absent: no model integration
# exists yet (SRS §7.4 is a later phase), so a key placeholder would be
# fiction. It will be added here when the provider adapter is built,
# sourced from the environment only (SRS NFR-013) and never written to
# traces or logs.
#
# `.env` is excluded by `.gitignore`; `.env.example` is tracked.
